Sval: removing the selected tab moves the selection even behind a modal

tabbrowser's selectedTab setter ignores a switch while a window-modal dialog
is open (window-modal-open). _blurTab goes through it, so a selected tab
removed then stays selected after its browser is gone, and every later
switch throws in AsyncTabSwitcher. Sval removes tabs behind its first-run
dialog when a chosen folder brings a document without them, and any removal
of the selected tab under such a dialog does the same. The guards keep the
user from switching tabs under a dialog; a removal must still leave a tab
that exists.

diff --git a/browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabbrowser.js b/browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabbrowser.js
index 19812924f2..e543eef46c 100644
--- a/browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabbrowser.js
+++ b/browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabbrowser.js
@@ -6332,7 +6332,9 @@
     }
 
     _blurTab(aTab) {
-      this.selectedTab = this._findTabToBlurTo(aTab);
+      // Not the selectedTab setter: it ignores a switch while a window-modal
+      // dialog is open, which would leave a removed tab selected.
+      this.tabbox.selectedTab = this._findTabToBlurTo(aTab);
     }
 
